cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the results it produces, please cite the paper below."
title: "Training-Data Provenance Governs the Cognitive Theories Encoded by Neural Models of Risky Choice — code and results"
abstract: >-
  Experimental framework that treats each trained neural network as a
  participant: models trained across provenance arms of human risky-choice data
  and across eight architectures are interrogated with a fixed battery of 1,742
  diagnostic problems, and reduced to four independent read-outs of the theory
  they encode. Includes the identifiability screens, design-sufficiency
  thresholds and artefact floors that make the comparison valid.
type: software
license: MIT
